# Mechatron Prime CI — Nix flake attributes the Thelio worker (x86_64-linux,
# thelio-nixos / mechatron-prime) builds on each signed push to yolo. Real
# attrs verified via `nix flake show`.
#
# The first two are exactly what `./test` runs: the unit+CLI test check and
# the package-build check.
checks.x86_64-linux.test
checks.x86_64-linux.build

# cross-windows added 2026-08-02. It is NOT run by `./test`, so before this it
# ran nowhere automatic — yet it is the check that catches vendored-openjpeg /
# musl / mingw linkage breakage, the exact class of failure that made adding
# the jpegz→jp2z dependency risky (jpegz vendors deps/openjpeg for this target
# and a sibling module with a hard `linkSystemLibrary` would have broken it).
#
# It is the slowest check in the repo and, unlike the other two, will not be a
# no-op when the developer has already run `./test` on the worker host. That
# cost is the point: a target that is always a cache hit verifies nothing new.
checks.x86_64-linux.cross-windows
checks.x86_64-linux.validator-closure
